# The vendored launcher is a verbatim copy, so git must not touch it.
#
# This repository has `core.autocrlf` on, which means every text file it tracks is
# stored with LF and checked out with CRLF. For our own code that is what we want.
# For `vendor/modrinth-app` it is not: a copy that has been re-ended is no longer
# the thing that was verified against, and `UPSTREAM.md` claims byte-for-byte.
#
# `-text` says "do not treat these as text": no end-of-line conversion on checkout
# and no normalisation on commit, so the bytes in the working tree are the bytes in
# the index are the bytes upstream shipped. It also stops diff from trying to show
# a line-ending change on 1857 files.
vendor/modrinth-app/** -text

# The bundled font faces are binary for the same reason. Inter's own files are
# ~300 KB of `glyf` and `cmap`, and a CRLF normalisation applied to them on a
# checkout would produce a file that still parses as a directory and renders
# nothing. `-text` keeps the bytes in the working tree the bytes in the index.
crates/palantir-desktop/assets/fonts/** -text
